  "summary": "Interpreting the candidate phrase \"decentralised training without pooled records\" as the federated-learning method in this candidate set, four supplied studies directly apply it to customer attrition: [V0203] reports AUROC 0.92 on Atlas-ICU; [V0201] reports accuracy 0.78 on ChurnBench; [V0204] reports test F1 0.64 on AgriSat-4; and [V0202] reports MAE 0.85 on MetroFlow. These results are not all like-for-like because accuracy, AUROC, F1, and MAE measure different things and MAE is an error metric. Prior-work mentions in [V0052], [V0045], and [V0101] are not applications and are excluded. Because exactly five IDs are required, [V0211] is appended only as a topic-matching customer-attrition comparator: it uses multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling rather than decentralised/federated training and reports 0.79 accuracy on Atlas-ICU.",
